Write a function sum_sat that takes two unsigned 32-bit numbers n and k and returns the sum, over every i from 0 to n - 1, of i * k saturated to 255 (a product above 255 counts as 255). The result is 0 when n is 0. Inputs always have n <= 100000. Write and use a helper function sat8(x) that turns an unsigned 32-bit number into an unsigned 8-bit number, giving 255 for anything above 255. Unsigned 32-bit arithmetic wraps around modulo 2^32 (it never traps).
